name: Link Analysis showcase
tagline: "A seeded Link Analysis demo - mule transfers with a planted ring, three landed days, staged next-day and gap-day files, five Demo Users, an index that builds itself and standing detection"
description: "The Link Analysis demo as a Space Template (LA-DEMO-SEED-1): a Basic tier with an Advanced tier on top. One daily Collector + Pipeline + Dataset of synthetic account-to-account transfers (data/inbox: three landed days; data/staged: a next-day file and a gap-day file you copy into the inbox by hand). The planted story: 12 SMURF accounts structure cash into MULE-HUB-01, which passes it on through RELAY-01/02 to OFFSHORE-77; SHELL-A to SHELL-D circulate money in a loop; TILL-06 takes 80 percent of the cash-out; SKIMMER-01 skims benefit payments. The Suspicion score ranks MULE-HUB-01 in the top 3 and the ring is the only directed cycle. Settings: link-analysis.toon (a low four-eyes fan-out threshold so expanding the hub waits for a second person, the link index ON, Drafts limits; masking_mode is left to the edition). Jobs: la_index_build (after every committed batch of the mule feed), la_detect (every 5 minutes) and mule_risk_score (every 10 minutes: the mule_account Risk Score - type mule_account into the Suspicion score's Risk Score model field to open per-node Factors; MULE-HUB-01 scores 100). Three saved views; the dashboard la_showcase_overview shows mule_layering_ring as a read-only Link analysis Widget. Demo Users and their roles (roles.toon, demo-users.toon): fm.analyst (lead; Author Alert Rules, Share and embed), fm.manager (second approver), ra.analyst (reviewer, read-only), demo.manager (not a member), admin (reveal). Investigations, members, Entity Lists, a Case and a bound Alert Rule are runtime state with no template home: run `node tools/seed-la-showcase.mjs --apply` against the running server (docs/okf/product/module/config/plan-spaces.md, section la-showcase). TELECOM corpus (config/telecom, data/inbox/<feed>; regenerate with tools/gen-la-telecom-data.py): eight 60-day feeds (voice_cdr, sms_cdr, hlr_eir, crm_kyc, recharge, provisioning, fraud_blocklist, fraud_alarms) over 2 400 background subscribers with one planted ring per typology (Wangiri, IRSF, SIM box, subscription fraud, mules) and a 650-caller supernode; the telecom_links Job folds them into one MSISDN-to-MSISDN link Dataset (seven link kinds) and telecom_msisdn_indicators scores every MSISDN 0-100; the suspect 99979100001 reaches the SIM box at degree 4 (docs/superpower/la-telecom-demo-data.md). GEO scene (synthetic, cities only): mule_account_locations places every account in a city, mule_geo_legs holds the stories' legs with both ends geocoded, and three saved Geo Views (mule_account_locations_map, mule_ring_route_map, mule_cashout_till_map) draw the ring from small-town branches through Rotterdam, Madrid and Warsaw to George Town and the cash-out converging on TILL-06 in Paris; regenerate with tools/gen-la-showcase-data.py. BASIC TIER (every edition, Basic included): the mule feed, the eight telecom feeds and the geo feeds with their Pipelines and Datasets, the telecom_links, telecom_msisdn_indicators and telecom_typology_counts Jobs, la_index_build, the pattern packs and the four saved views; masking_mode is left to the edition, so a Basic build, where nobody signs in, shows every id. Standard and above add the three saved Geo Views (Geo map) and the dashboard's Link analysis Widget. ADVANCED TIER (a sign-in build; inert on Basic): typed masking with the admin's audited Reveal, four-eyes and Drafts, la_detect (with no Alert Rule bound it evaluates nothing), the mule_account Risk Score and its mule_risk_score Job, the three telecom Alert Rules (telecom_wangiri_lines, telecom_irsf_lines, telecom_simbox_lines) and their telecom_typology_alerts Job, which ship unarmed where Alert Rules are absent, the Demo Users and roles, and the seed script's runtime state; the walk-through needs an Advanced or Preview edition build with Demo Auth (serve-demo). Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:share
contents[12]: "Pipeline + schema (daily partition) with 3 landed days", "Dataset", "3 saved views", "8 telecom Pipelines with 60-day extracts and planted fraud rings", "telecom_links + telecom_msisdn_indicators Jobs, Datasets and a saved view", "link-analysis.toon (index ON; typed masking, four-eyes and Drafts on sign-in builds)", "la_index_build Job (on pipeline.commit)", "la_detect Job (cron; Advanced tier, evaluates nothing on Basic)", "mule_account Risk Score + mule_risk_score Job (Suspicion score Factors; Advanced tier)", "5 Demo Users + role table (Advanced tier, inert on Basic)", "Staged next-day and gap-day files", "GEO scene: 113 synthetic account locations, geocoded story legs, 3 saved Geo Views (Standard and above)"
